---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const seoTitle = 'The Best Whisky Alternative for Mac (2026): One Click, No Bottles';
const description =
  'Whisky stopped getting updates in 2025. Pixel Port is the one-click way to keep playing Windows games on your Mac. No bottles, no winetricks, no terminal.';

const canonical = new URL('/whisky-alternative/', Astro.site).toString();
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Article',
      headline: 'The best Whisky alternative for Mac in 2026',
      description,
      url: canonical,
      author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Pixel Port' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', Astro.site).toString() },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Whisky alternative', item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
};

const rows = [
  { tool: 'Whisky', setup: 'Manual bottles + winetricks', upkeep: 'Discontinued in 2025', cls: 'text-muted' },
  { tool: 'CrossOver', setup: 'Mostly manual', upkeep: 'Maintained', cls: 'text-muted' },
  { tool: 'Pixel Port', setup: 'One click', upkeep: 'Actively maintained', cls: 'text-fg font-semibold' },
];
---

<Base title={seoTitle} description={description}>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} slot="head" />

  <article class="wrap py-16 sm:py-24">
    <nav class="text-sm text-muted">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-fg">Home</a> <span class="px-1">/</span> Whisky alternative
    </nav>

    <h1 class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-balance text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
      The best Whisky alternative for Mac
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted">
      Whisky, the Wine wrapper a lot of Mac gamers relied on, stopped getting updates in 2025.
      Pixel Port is the one-click way to keep playing Windows games on your Mac, and it does the
      setup for you.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <a
        href="/download"
        class="inline-block rounded-full bg-linear-to-r from-accent to-accent-2 px-7 py-3.5 font-semibold text-white shadow-[var(--shadow-glow)] [text-shadow:0_1px_2px_rgba(10,8,22,0.4)] transition-[transform,filter] hover:brightness-110 active:scale-[0.98]"
      >
        Download Pixel Port
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-14 max-w-2xl prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-accent-2">
      <h2>What happened to Whisky?</h2>
      <p>
        Whisky was an open-source wrapper around Wine that made it easier to run Windows games on
        Apple Silicon. In 2025 its developer stepped back and the project was discontinued. It still
        launches for some people, but it no longer receives updates, compatibility fixes, or support for
        new versions of macOS. And even at its best, Whisky still asked you to create bottles, install
        the right dependencies by hand, and troubleshoot when a game would not start.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Pixel Port is the natural successor</h2>
      <p>
        Pixel Port removes the thing people did not love about Whisky: the manual setup. You install
        Pixel Port once, pick a game, and click. Our bundled
        runtime, Prism, translates the game's DirectX calls straight to Metal, and the Synthesis Engine
        works out how each game should run on your Mac automatically. No bottles to manage, no winetricks,
        no terminal.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is also kept current. Because our Distributed Validation Network learns from real launches on
        real Macs, the catalogue gets more reliable over time instead of going stale.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Whisky vs CrossOver vs Pixel Port</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-surface/60 text-muted">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Tool</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Setup</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-medium">Upkeep</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-line">
          {
            rows.map((r) => (
              <tr class={r.tool === 'Pixel Port' ? 'bg-accent/10' : 'bg-surface/30'}>
                <td class={`px-5 py-4 ${r.cls}`}>{r.tool}</td>
                <td class="px-5 py-4 text-fg/85">{r.setup}</td>
                <td class="px-5 py-4 text-fg/85">{r.upkeep}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 rounded-3xl border border-accent/25 bg-linear-to-br from-accent/15 to-accent-2/10 p-10 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Switch in one click</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-lg text-muted">
        Download Pixel Port, find your game in the catalogue, and play. That is the whole migration.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/download"
        class="mt-7 inline-block rounded-full bg-linear-to-r from-accent to-accent-2 px-8 py-4 text-lg font-semibold text-white shadow-[var(--shadow-glow)] [text-shadow:0_1px_2px_rgba(10,8,22,0.4)] transition-[transform,filter] hover:brightness-110 active:scale-[0.98]"
      >
        Download for Mac
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
